      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Adequate myocardial protection is difficult to achieve during operations for combined aortic valve disease and severe stenosis of the left main coronary artery. A double cross-clamp technique, which facilitates the delivery of cardioplegic solution to the myocardium, is described here. We reviewed the experiences of 11 patients, 6 of whom underwent operation using the new technique."},
